Rzarrs includes Rust dependencies vendored for reproducible source builds.

The Rust dependency source archive at src/rust/vendor.tar.xz is generated from
src/rust/Cargo.lock with `cargo vendor`. Copyright and license files for each
vendored crate are preserved inside that archive. The package Authors@R records
"Authors of the dependency Rust crates" as copyright holders for these bundled
third-party sources.

Major upstream projects used by the Rust implementation include:

- zarrs and related zarrs_* crates: https://github.com/zarrs/zarrs
- zarrs_object_store / object_store integration: https://github.com/apache/arrow-rs
- savvy: https://github.com/yutannihilation/savvy
- tokio: https://tokio.rs/
- serde / serde_json: https://serde.rs/
- flate2: https://github.com/rust-lang/flate2-rs

See src/rust/Cargo.lock for exact crate names and versions.
